I18N NOTE (honesty / no silent drift): the 37 coverage.* keys did not previously exist in the canonical
web i18n source (web/src/i18n/en.json — the web page used inline t(key, fallback) defaults). They were
added to en.json (canonical, durable) AND to apps/android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml as
translation_coverage_*. A FULL re-run of gen-i18n.ts was deliberately NOT performed: the generated
catalog is already ~194 keys behind en.json on this integration branch (pre-existing committed drift),
so a full regen would sweep hundreds of unrelated keys across apple/windows/catalog. The hand-added
android entries were verified byte-for-byte against gen-i18n.ts's own androidName + renderValue logic
(expected=37 actual=37 mismatches=0), so they introduce ZERO coverage-specific drift; the pre-existing
194-key catalog drift is untouched and out of scope. lint disables MissingTranslation (placeholder
ar/he locales are English fallback), so values/ is sufficient.

